  "term": "clinical neurology",
  "definition": "Acromegaly is a condition in adults caused by long-term exposure to too much human growth hormone. It leads to enlargement of the bones of the face, lower jaw, hands, feet, head, and chest, most often because of a pituitary adenoma that secretes growth hormone.",
